    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n57413" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κιμμέριοι</span></b> , οἱ,
			<u>Cimmerians</u>, a mythical people dwelling beyond the
		Ocean in perpetual darkness, <i><span class="en">
			Od.
			11.14
		</span></i>; later, a nomad people of the steppes, who invaded Asia Minor,
			<i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			1.15
		</span></i>, etc.:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κίμμεροι</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Lyc.
			695
		</span></i>:—Adj.
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κιμμερικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
			<u>Cimmerian</u>: K. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσθμός</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the Crimea</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				730
			</span></i>; K. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βόσπορος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					1.1.10
				</span></i>
			, al.:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κιμμέριος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.12
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Κιμμερίη</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ</span>) ibid.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κιμμερίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>, ἡ, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				478
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
				2.1.3
			</span></i>.</div>
